    "OT_VERSE_SNIPPET": "Not by might, nor by power, but by my spirit, saith the LORD of hosts.",
    "NT_VERSE_REF": "2 Corinthians 3:17",
    "NT_VERSE_SNIPPET": "Now the Lord is that Spirit: and where the Spirit of the Lord is, there is liberty.",
    "OT_VERSE_LINE": "Zechariah 4:6 — “Not by might, nor by power, but by my spirit, saith the LORD of hosts.”",
    "NT_VERSE_LINE": "2 Corinthians 3:17 — “Now the Lord is that Spirit: and where the Spirit of the Lord is, there is liberty.”",
    "GREEK": "πνεῦμα",
    "GREEK_TRANSLIT": "Pneuma",
    "HEBREW": "רוּחַ",
    "HEBREW_TRANSLIT": "Ruach",
    "OT_REFS": "Gen 1:2 • Num 11:25 • Isa 11:2 • Ezek 37:14 • Joel 2:28",
    "NT_REFS": "Matt 3:16 • John 3:5 • Acts 2:4 • Rom 8:14 • Gal 5:22",
    "TRIVIA_BULLETS": [
      "The Hebrew 'ruach' and Greek 'pneuma' both translate to 'wind,' 'breath,' and 'spirit.'",
      "Scripture uses symbols like a dove, fire, oil, and wind to describe the Spirit's invisible work.",
      "The Spirit is the agent of creation in Genesis and the agent of new creation in the Gospels."
